Legacy variants (pre-3.14.0) of this flask use {{c|crafted|crafted mods}} which have a different color than {{c|augmented|normal mods}}. These crafted mods can be removed from the unique item but are not able to be crafted back via the [[Crafting Bench]], effectively bricking the item. The mod text and mod value are the same between the crafted mod and the new, 3.14 introduced unveil mod.

The version dropped during [[version 3.5.0]] ([[Betrayal league]]) has a lower required character level to equip (40). The new versions require character level 48, as the level of the crafted/unveil mods are level 60 (60 times 0.8 = 48).

Players can create a quasi-legacy variant by obtaining a veiled legacy Cinderswallow Urn, and unveiling a currently obtainable mod on the flask.

==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.26.0|
* The Veiled Modifiers on the Mastermind's Unique Items are now able to unveil some new modifiers that are exclusive to these Uniques.
* Cinderswallow Urn's veiled modifier is now a prefix, and can roll exclusive "Catarina's" modifiers. This affects existing veiled and unveiled items. This does not affect legacy versions that have the crafted version of veiled modifiers from before [[version 3.14.0]]; these are still suffixes.{{efn|name=Misnamed prefixes}} {{Undocumented}}
* Cinderswallow Urn now has +(10-20) to Maximum Charges (previously +90). {{Undocumented}}
* Cinderswallow Urn no longer has (175-200)% increased Charges per use. {{Undocumented}}
}}
{{Version history table row|3.24.0|
* The Veiled modifier that provides reduced Mana Cost of Skills during Effect can no longer be unveiled or crafted on Flasks.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.21.0|
* The Unique Item drop chances for Catarina, Master of Undeath have been rebalanced.
* Can now drop from any level of the Catarina encounter. {{Undocumented}}
}}
{{Version history table row|3.16.0|
* The Cinderswallow Urn Unique Flask has changed as a result of the [[Version 3.16.0#Flasks|changes to flasks]]. "{{c|mod|60-80% reduced Reflected Damage taken during Flask Effect}}" is now a possible modifier when Unveiling this Flask, which has replaced the increased Critical Strike Chance during Flask Effect modifier that was possible previously. The crafted version of this new modifier has values of 45-55%, and has replaced the Critical Strike Chance during Flask Effect crafting option.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.15.0|
* Cinderswallow Urn now spawns with either '{{c|mod|Recover 1-3% Life when you kill an enemy during flask effect}}', '{{c|mod|Recover 1-3% Mana when you kill an enemy during flask effect}}' or '{{c|mod|Recover 1-3% Energy Shield when you kill an enemy during flask effect}}'.
* Cinderswallow Urn now has {{c|mod|+90 to maximum Charges}}, and has {{c|mod|175-200% increased Charges Used}}.
* Cinderswallow Urn now {{c|mod|recharges 5 Charges when you consume an ignited corpse}} (previously 1), 
* Cinderswallow Urn now has {{c|mod|Enemies ignited during flask effect now take 7-10% increased damage}} (previously 10%).
* The Veiled/crafted Flask Suffix that gives {{c|mod|increased Critical Strike Chance during Flask Effect}}, now grants 40-60% (previously 60-80%).
* The Veiled/crafted Flask Suffix that gives {{c|mod|50% Chance to Avoid Being Stunned During Flask Effect}} and {{c|mod|8-12% increased Movement Speed during Flask Effect}}, no longer grants movement speed during Flask Effect.{{efn|name=Legacy modifier JunMasterLocalFlaskAvoidStunChanceAndMovementSpeedDuringFlaskEffect1}}
* Silver Flask now lasts 4 seconds (previously 5). Now requires level 40 to use (previously level 22).
}}
{{Version history table row|3.14.1|
* Fixed a bug where the Cinderswallow Urn unique flask wasn't applying the correct ignite visual.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.14.0c|
* Fixed a bug where the "{{c|mod|8-12% increased Movement Speed during Flask Effect}}" veiled modifier was not being granted alongside the "{{c|mod|50% Chance to avoid being Stunned during Flask Effect}}" veiled modifier. Existing items can obtain the missing modifier by using a Divine Orb.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.14.0|
* Modifiers that are unveiled through Jun are now more powerful than before. Previously, when an item was unveiled, the veiled modifier added to the item would be equal to the highest tier modifier available on the Crafting Bench. Now, the modifier being unveiled no longer counts as a crafted modifier and will be stronger than any craftable veiled modifier.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.6.0|
